# PR/PO Approval — Gate 0 Decisions

**Status:** DESIGN PROPOSALS FOR REVIEW. **Unresolved owner items are listed explicitly.**  
**Local HEAD:** `03a142cc186efe25918523537c844b14e232971a`  
**Not implemented.** No posting, stock, approval engine, or database source was changed for Gate 0.

These decisions **supersede** conflicting v2/v3 wording. They do **not** authorize Gate 1–3.

---

## D1. Policy publication linearization (V4-C2) — PROPOSED

**Evidence:** [`SavePolicyAsync`](../ErpWeb.Core/Purchase/ProcurementApprovalService.cs) 109–217 begins a transaction, reads published policy with ordinary `LoadPublishedPolicyAsync` (1315–1321), unpublishes, inserts `Version+1`, commits. [`AssertGateAsync`](../ErpWeb.Core/Purchase/ProcurementApprovalService.cs) 1087–1114 reads the same published row **without** that lock. GR/NG holds a PO row lock, which does **not** serialize against settings.

**Mechanism:** copy the proven [`BranchStockTransactionLock`](../ErpWeb.Core/StockLedger/BranchStockTransactionLock.cs) pattern (`sys.sp_getapplock`, Exclusive, Transaction, 15s timeout, fail closed).

- Resource: `PO_APPR_POLICY|{COMPANY}|{DOCTYPE}` (uppercase trimmed). Company in the name prevents cross-tenant collision on a shared SQL instance.
- **Publisher:** acquire lock **before** `LoadPublishedPolicyAsync`; hold until commit. First-enable (no row) is still serialized because the resource exists without a table row.
- **Authoritative gates** (Submit, PR convert `AssertPrConvertibleAsync` under PO save, GR/NG `AssertPoReceivableAsync`, Force Close `AssertPoCloseableAsync`): acquire **after** document header locks, **before** reading published policy / asserting the gate.
- **Publisher must not acquire PR/PO headers.** That avoids policy→header inversion vs guards that take headers first.
- Timeout (`sp_getapplock` result &lt; 0): fail closed, retryable: `Approval settings are being updated. Retry the command.`
- Ordinary READ COMMITTED is **not** sufficient.

**Expected races:**

| Scenario | Outcome |
|----------|---------|
| Two `SavePolicyAsync` | One waits; exactly one new published version; no two `IsPublished=1` for same company+docType |
| Enable vs fresh GR of NEW unapproved PO | Enable wins lock first → GR sees ON and must have a valid gate; or GR wins first and completes under previous OFF **only if** it already held policy lock before enable — serialized so no stale OFF after enable commits |
| Disable vs Pending | Pending still blocks (`AssertGateAsync` 1093–1096). Disable must not unlock in-flight cycles |
| Submit vs new policy version | Submit snapshots `PolicyId`/`PolicyVersion` (1003–1012); in-flight instance unchanged |
| OFF regression | Real guard returns permit when no published enabled policy **and** no Pending instance |

**Schema:** none required if applock is used. Unique `(CompanyCode, DocType, Version)` already exists ([`create-po-approval.sql`](../scripts/create-po-approval.sql) 32–34). Consider a filtered unique published index later (separate schema approval) — not required to start if applock is proven.

**Owner sign-off:** accept applock resource names and timeout message. **STOP if** a shared lock cannot be proven against existing branch-stock + document lock graphs (see PATH_LOCK_MATRIX global order).

