## D2. Latest PO revision (V4-C1) — PROPOSED

**Evidence:** [`LockLatestForUpdateAsync`](../ErpWeb.Model/Repositories/Purchase/PoOrderRepository.cs) 136–149 = unlocked `GetMaxRelNoAsync` then `LockForUpdateAsync`. Callers: PO save/revise ~1023, `LockRequestedPoAsync` ~1416, GR PO lock ~4210.

**Do not** claim the current PO row lock serializes revise vs GR.

**Minimal strategy (prefer not rewriting every `LockLatestForUpdateAsync` caller blindly):**

1. New helper used by **GR/NG NEW-post** and **PO Revise** (audit all three callers before widening): acquire `PO_REV|{COMPANY}|{BRANCH}|{PONO}` Exclusive Transaction **before** reading max RelNo.
2. `LockForUpdateAsync` on that RelNo.
3. **Recheck** `Max(PoRelNo)` inside the same transaction; if it differs, fail closed with `Purchase Order was revised. Reload and select the latest approved revision.`
4. Then policy lock + instance lock + `AssertPoReceivableAsync` on the **locked** RelNo.
5. Existing qty validator still rejects draft lines whose `PoRelNo` ≠ locked latest.

Cancelled old revisions may help but are **secondary**. SQL barrier tests in PATH_LOCK_MATRIX R1–R6 are mandatory before claiming correctness.

**Owner sign-off:** apply the applock to revise + GR/NG post in Gate 1; other `LockLatest` callers in the same Gate 1 PR after the three-site audit.

---

## D3. Progressed-document grandfathering (V4-H1) — PRESERVE (explicit)

**Evidence:** `AssertGateAsync` 1155–1162 permits documents with `RecvQty > 0` or PO Received/Closed, or PR derived ordered / PO-link consumption.

**Product decision proposed:** **keep current grandfathering.** A PO that already had a physical receipt **before** enablement may post **remaining** quantity after enablement without a new approval. A **truly NEW** unapproved PO (`RecvQty = 0`, not Received/Closed) **must not** receive its first GR when policy is ON.

This is **not** a silent tightening of v3 “no new commitment after enable.” Remaining-qty and status formulas stay unchanged.

**PENDING still blocks when policy is OFF** (1093–1096). Do not change.

**APPROVED / NOT_REQUIRED** remain snapshot-based (`PolicyId`, `PolicyVersion`, fingerprint, assignees). Policy edits do not recompute them.

**Owner sign-off required:** confirm remaining GR after enablement on a partially received PO is intended. If business wants to freeze remaining qty behind approval, that is a **separate** signed rule change.

---

## D4. Trusted cutover timestamps (V4-H2) — FAIL CLOSED ON UNTRUSTED FALLBACK

**Evidence:**

- Policy `CutoverAtUtc` assigned `DateTime.UtcNow` (`SavePolicyAsync` 135, 157–159).
- PR/PO `CreatedDate` assigned `_dates.Now` which is **company-local** ([`CurrentDateService`](../ErpWeb.Core/Services/CurrentDateService.cs) 13–35, never blind UtcNow). EF maps to column `Created` ([`PoPrConfiguration`](../ErpWeb.Model/Configurations/Purchase/PoPrConfiguration.cs) 35, [`PoOrderConfiguration`](../ErpWeb.Model/Configurations/Purchase/PoOrderConfiguration.cs) 88).
- Gate fallback: `CreatedDate ?? CreateDt` (PR) or `CreatedDate ?? PoDate` (PO) at 1135 / 1148. `CreateDt` / `PoDate` (`PODt`) are **editable business dates**.

**Local DEMO sample (redacted):** 0 null `Created` on 27 PR / 14 PO rows. That does **not** prove other tenants.

**Decision:**

1. Cutover / LegacyExempt may use **`Created` (CreatedDate) converted to UTC using the document company timezone**, compared to `CutoverAtUtc`.
2. If `Created` is null: **fail closed** (require submit/approval) — do **not** treat `PoDate`/`CreateDt` as proof of pre-enablement.
3. Current published DEMO mode is `REQUIRE_GOING_FORWARD` (LegacyExempt path inactive unless switched). Timestamp mixing still must be fixed before enabling LegacyExempt.
4. Kind-unaware `createdAt < cutover` (local 10:00 vs UTC 02:33) is **untrusted**.

**Owner sign-off:** UTC conversion helper vs requiring a backfill migration of `Created`. **Unresolved** until signed. Gate 1 GR guard can ship **without** changing LegacyExempt if mode remains RequireGoingForward, but must not expand the untrusted fallback.

---

## D5. NEW backdated post vs historical replay vs repair (V4-H3) — CLASSIFIED

| Root | Approval |
|------|----------|
| Fast `PostGoodsReceiptAsync` stock GR and NG, RecvQty +1 | **Gate NEW-post** |
| WAC/Standard/FIFO **NEW** backdated methods that lock PO and apply RecvQty +1 on a NEW batch | **Gate NEW-post** (do not exempt because the class name contains Replay) |
| GR rollback, VR, historical revaluation/removal of **already posted** descendants | **No first-time approval gate** |
| `PurchaseGoodsReceiptRepairAdapter.RepostAsync` (CostingRepairAdapters.cs 293–299) | Calls public `_posting.PostAsync`. Context unused. **No tamper-resistant proof.** |

**Repair decision:** **no public `skipApproval`**. **no caller-name exemption.** Until a signed internal repair-context design exists, repair repost is a **normal NEW post** and must pass `AssertPoReceivableAsync`. Costing repair of a fully rolled-back PO (RecvQty=0) will require a current approval if policy is ON; progressed grandfathering still applies if RecvQty&gt;0 remains.

**Owner sign-off:** accept “repair is not exempt” **or** commission a separate repair-proof design. **STOP** for any bypass that a user can trigger with a batch number.

---

## D6. Decision / withdraw lock order (V4-H4) — PROPOSED

Today: `DecideAsync` 325 instance-first then reads creator/consumption; `WithdrawAsync` 460 same; PR/PO save document-first; GR PO-header-first.

**Required for Decide / Withdraw / Return** (any path that reads creator, fingerprint, or consumption):

1. Nonlocking lookup instance by ID → `(Company, Branch, DocType, DocNo, DocRev)`
2. Validate tenant
3. Lock exact PR or PO header
4. Lock instance by ID; re-fetch
5. Revalidate company/branch/key/revision/rowversion/status
6. Compare fingerprint / consumption from **locked** document
7. Decision + event same commit

Missing/stale document → fail closed. **Never** treat `CurrentFingerprintAsync == null` as approved (V4-M1) on a path that did not just lock the document.

`ReassignAsync`: remain instance-only **if** Gate 1 code review confirms it still never touches PR/PO.

PR Return/Withdraw consumption: use existing `IsPrConsumed` / `RecvQty` under the **PR** lock. Do not lock PO after PR unless the global matrix is shared by all writers. **No new remaining-qty engine.**

---

## D7. PR picker (V4-H5) — READ-ONLY EVALUATOR

Today: Take(100) then `IsPrVisibleForPoAsync` → `AssertGateAsync`, which can `Add` cutover exemption/event (1168–1194). Picker DbContext does not `SaveChanges` (tracked entities, not proven persisted).

**Decision:**

- Extract a **side-effect-free** `EvaluatePrConvertibleReadOnly` sharing Pending / Approved / NotRequired / progressed / exemption **read** / cutover **compare** predicates — **zero** `DbContext.Add`.
- Chunked stable sort (existing CreateDt/PrNo desc); fetch windows; batch-load instances/exemptions; filter; stop at 100 eligible.
- Persist cutover evidence **only** in PO Save under `LockConsumptionAsync` + policy lock, once.
- `GetPrRemainingLinesAsync` stays advisory; PO Save `AssertPrConvertibleAsync` stays authoritative.
- Do not duplicate remaining-qty math.

---

## D8. Attachments (V4-H6) — CHOICE A (document-wide freeze)

**Evidence:** `StampAttachRevNoAsync` 2594–2600 restamps **all** rows for `DocId=PoNo`. Upload uses unlocked max RelNo. Files outside SQL.

**Choice A (selected for this plan; no schema):**

- Document-wide attachment set. **Do not claim** per-revision historical snapshots.
- After the **first submitted cycle** (Pending/Approved/NotRequired) on any revision of that PO, **prohibit delete/replace**. **Additions** on a later **draft** revision: **owner must confirm**. Conservative default: **no delete/replace**; **allow add** only while no Pending/Approved instance exists on **any** revision (i.e. returned/withdrawn/new draft after close of cycle).
- UI must show the limitation (separate Settings/UI PR — do not implement here).
- Temp promotion (`StampAttachDocIdsInDbAsync`, `MoveDraftSafeAsync`) must not bypass the freeze.
- **Choice B** (immutable revision snapshots) needs additive schema and a **distinct** review — not this Gate.

**File I/O (reconciled):**

1. Stream + magic-byte validation to a unique temp file **before** any PR/PO `UPDLOCK`.
2. Short SQL transaction: reauthorize; lock current PR or latest PO (after PO_REV applock); lock instance; duplicate/quota; insert/remove metadata.
3. **Documented exception:** a **same-volume atomic `File.Move`/`Replace`** of an already-staged local file may occur immediately before `SaveChanges` (bounded, not a network stream).
4. On DB rollback: delete the staged final file if it was moved in. Never delete the user’s only copy after a failed commit.
5. Delete path: remove metadata, **commit**, then physical delete with retry + recorded orphan cleanup. Never delete file before successful DB commit.

---

## D9. Fingerprint (V4-H7) — PRESERVE V1 (instances exist)

**Local DEMO inventory (2026-11-02, redacted):** `PoApprovalInstance` = **7 PENDING + 3 APPROVED** PR rows, fingerprint length 64 (SHA256 hex). **In-place algorithm change is forbidden.**

**V1 hashed today** ([`ProcurementApprovalFingerprint`](../ErpWeb.Core/Purchase/ProcurementApprovalFingerprint.cs)):

- PR: PrType, DeptCode, ProjId, LocationCode; line Line, ICode, PurchaseQty, UnitPrice, Amount, Currency, TaxGroup, TaxAmount, IsInclusive, VendorCd, PaymentTerm, BuyingTerm.
- PO: VendCode, CurCode, TermCode, BuyingTerm, Discount, TaxGrpCode, ShipCode, ShipName; line Line, ICode, PoPurQty, PoUnitPrice, NetAmount, TaxAmount, ItemDiscount, DiscountType, ItemDiscount1, DiscountType1, PrNo, PrLineNo.

**Material fields omitted (do not hash operational qty):** PurchaseUom/StdUom, ToWarehouse, Dept/Proj/Location on PO header, line TaxGroup/IsInclusive on PO, PoQty vs PoPurQty, service/stock IType, ETA, addresses, remarks, RecvQty/ReturnQty/InvoicedQty.

**Decision:** Keep V1 for **all existing and new cycles** until a signed V2 (fingerprint version column = schema exception + rollout). Submit, Decide (after document lock), and downstream guards must call the **same** V1 `ForPr`/`ForPo`. Never silently rehash stored rows. Never hash RecvQty/ReturnQty/InvoicedQty or regenerate totals.

**V4-M1:** If `CurrentFingerprintAsync` returns null (missing document), **fail closed** at gates that did not lock the document. Do not treat null as matching APPROVED.

**Owner sign-off:** V2 field list and schema later; **not** Gate 1.

