## D10. Mandatory DI (preview for Gate 2)

Production constructors take non-null `IProcurementApprovalGuard`. DI already maps both interfaces ([`CoreServiceCollectionExtensions`](../ErpWeb.Core/CoreServiceCollectionExtensions.cs) 347–348). Missing registration → startup fail. Test-only disabled stub **only** in explicit policy-OFF unit harnesses. **Never** in production DI. Policy OFF behavior stays inside the **real** guard.

Uncommitted nullable injection on posting/GR services is **not** the Gate 1 design.

---

## D11. Invoice / CDN

**No new invoice/CDN approval gates.** `ValidateMatchOnPostAsync` 1633–1637 rejects non-CN invoice when net received ≤ 0. CDN does not write RecvQty. Self-billed has no PO lineage. Service-only first commitment is **NG post** (D5), not Force Close. Force Close remains stock-remainder + existing `AssertPoCloseableAsync`. Direct non-PO invoices stay out of this gate.

---

## D12. User-facing messages (preview)

- Blocked GR/NG: `Purchase Order {PoNo} needs approval before this receipt can be posted.`
- Stale revision: `Purchase Order was revised. Reload and select the latest approved revision.`
- Policy lock timeout: `Approval settings are being updated. Retry the command.`
- No hashes, SQL, CostLayer, or lock jargon.

---

## D13. Deploy sequence (preview — not executed)

1. Idempotent `scripts/create-po-approval.sql` + `scripts/init-po-approval-menu.sql` on **each** tenant DB **before** mandatory-guard binaries.
2. Verify filtered unique `UX_PoApprovalInstance_Active` (SQL script has it; **EF mapping does not** — uniqueness is SQL-enforced when script applied).
3. Deploy code with policy **OFF**; smoke PR/PO/GR/NG/rollback/VR.
4. Enable per tenant.
5. Missing approval tables at runtime → **clear no-post + operator alert**, not silent OFF.
6. Feature-off leaves Pending locked. Code rollback preserves audit and stock/cost.

**This checkout:** single `DefaultConnection` (no multi-tenant catalog in `Program.cs`). Live tenant inventory is the local `ERPWeb` database only (see TEST_BASELINE). Other deployed servers were **not** reachable from this investigation.

